<title>UK: GKN shares drop as profit-takers move in.</title>
<headline>GKN shares drop as profit-takers move in.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in GKN Plc stalled on Wednesday as some investors cashed in on recent gains in the automotive and engineering group, dealers said.</p>
<p>The stock was down 23-1/2p or 2.2 percent at 10.26-1/2 stg by 1354 GMT, the third biggest decliner in the FTSE 100 index. Volume reached 1.1 million shares.</p>
<p>&quot;There has been a big squeeze upwards in recent sessions and all of a sudden a few sellers have appeared,&quot; said one market-maker.</p>
<p>GKN shares touched a five-month high of 10.69 stg on May 30.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
